==== Opening the case ====

**Note:** This will void your warranty!

  - Remove the two top rubber feet on left and right as shown on the picture
{{:media:asus:rt-ax53u:asus_rt-ax53u-back-casing.jpg?400|}}
  - unscrew two screws that are sitting below the rubber feet casings, right one has a warranty sign
  - use a metal pry tool and start opening form the lower part of the bottom casing (opposite side of the LEDs), slide the plier carefully around the unit in order to remove the top cover
  - you now have access to the pcb and can move onto the soldering part

